  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Not metabolized by the cytochrome P450 system, and 52% of an intravenous dose is recovered unchanged in urine within 24 hours.",
    "substance": "A synthetic compound supplied as an acetate salt trihydrate, with molecular weight 1069.2 for the active moiety.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA in single-dose ampules and multiple-dose vials, dosed as one or two divided doses daily.",
    "safety": "Boxed warning for severe hyponatremia, which can be life-threatening. Contraindicated with hyponatremia, SIADH or polydipsia; nausea and abdominal cramps are reported.",
    "indication": "Replacement therapy for central diabetes insipidus and temporary polyuria after head trauma or pituitary surgery; bleeding in hemophilia A and von Willebrand's disease type I.",
    "mechanism": "Stimulates V2 receptors, increasing water reabsorption in the kidney, and raises factor VIII activity in hemophilia and von Willebrand's disease."
  },
  "tell": "Its factor VIII-raising effect for bleeding disorders, beyond its antidiuretic action, sets it apart.",
